.env
.env.local
.env.*
# The two lines above correctly keep real secrets (.env, infra/.env, any
# .env.local) out of git -- but .env.* also matched .env.example and
# infra/.env.example, the two template files README.md's "Getting
# started" tells a fresh clone to copy from. Neither file was ever
# actually in the repository because of this: `git log --all` has zero
# commits touching either path. Un-ignore them explicitly.
!.env.example
!infra/.env.example
node_modules/

# Go build cache (used for sandboxed builds)
.gocache/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor / OS cruft (defensive -- none currently tracked, keep it that way)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db

# Go test/coverage artifacts, in case a local `go test -cover` run drops
# one of these inside the tree instead of /tmp
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Internal working docs from the development/audit process (bug lists,
# gap audits, phased build plans, the pre-build vision doc) -- useful
# during the build, not meant to ship in the judged submission. The
# curated, judge-facing doc set is what README.md's own "Docs" section
# links to (files/AUTH.md, GIT-WORKFLOW.md, agent-commerce-contract.md,
# trust-boundary.md, pitch-one-pager.md, demo-script.md); none of those
# are affected. Note: dozens of code comments across backend/ and
# frontend/ still cite these filenames (e.g. "PLAN-05-SELLER-DASHBOARD.md
# §4") as internal design notes -- those citations are now unresolvable
# from inside the repo, a deliberate tradeoff for a cleaner file tree.
files/BUGS.md
files/AUDIT-2026-08-29.md
files/REALITY-CHECK-2026-08-30.md
files/ROADMAP-PRIORITIZED.md
files/ORIGINAL-VISION-AUTONOMOUS-REVENUE-AGENT.md
files/ORIGINAL-VISION-BUILD-GUIDE.md
files/PLAN-01-AGENTIC-CORE.md
files/PLAN-02-CATALOG-AND-COMMERCE.md
files/PLAN-03-PROACTIVE-GROWTH-AGENT.md
files/PLAN-04-UI-UX-AND-LATENCY.md
files/PLAN-05-SELLER-DASHBOARD.md
files/PLAN-06-ADDITIONAL-OPPORTUNITIES.md
